---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const links = [
  ['/install/', 'Install & run', 'Build from source and load the unpacked Chromium extension.'],
  [
    '/how-it-works/',
    'The review workflow',
    'Profiles, suggestions, selection, filling, memories and undo.',
  ],
  ['/privacy/', 'Privacy & data', 'What stays local and what the website can read after filling.'],
  [
    '/limitations/',
    'Controls & troubleshooting',
    'Supported controls, page-access errors and dynamic forms.',
  ],
  [
    '/benchmarks/',
    'Benchmark & methodology',
    'Real measured results on labelled synthetic examples.',
  ],
  [
    '/articles/',
    'Engineering field notes',
    'Reusable profiles, privacy boundaries and visible uncertainty.',
  ],
];
---

<Layout
  title="FormPilot documentation"
  description="Installation, review workflow, local data handling, compatibility and reproducible benchmark documentation for the open-source FormPilot extension."
>
  <div class="page-heading">
    <h1>A useful tool should be understandable.</h1>
    <p>Start with installation, or look closer at the decisions behind the fill button.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-grid">
    {links.map(([url, title, text]) => (
      <a class="doc-link" href={url}>
        <h2 style="font-size:22px">{title}</h2>
        <p>{text}</p>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>For contributors</h2>
    <p>
      The repository includes architecture and threat-model documents, labelled fixtures, DOM
      integration tests and real extension browser tests. Run <code>npm run check</code>,{' '}
      <code>npm run test:e2e</code> and <code>npm run benchmark</code> from the repository root.
      CONTRIBUTING.md explains the expectations for adding aliases, controls and tests.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
